+# Sources consulted
+
+Accessed 2026-08-14 with live network requests.
+
+- Broadcom Product Interoperability Matrix, Upgrade Path for VMware Cloud Foundation: https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Upgrade?productId=114 — checked that the submitted milestone choices should be assessed as product upgrade-path decisions rather than inferred from version numbers.
+- Broadcom Knowledge Base 405275, “Upgrade VMware Cloud Foundation (VCF) 4.x and 5.x”: https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/405275/upgrade-vmware-cloud-foundation-vcf-4x-a.html — confirmed prechecks and the SDDC Manager, Aria, NSX, vCenter, ESX component sequence.
+- Broadcom Knowledge Base 313502, “VCF 5.0.x is not a supported upgrade path if you are running VCF 4.5.2”: https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/313502/vcf-50x-is-not-a-supported-upgrade-path.html — confirmed that 4.5.2 must not be routed through 5.0.x.
+- VMware Cloud Foundation Blog, “Using vSphere Supervisor? Here’s a Comprehensive Guide to Upgrading to VCF 5.2.1”: https://blogs.vmware.com/cloud-foundation/2025/04/08/using-vsphere-supervisor-heres-a-comprehensive-guide-to-upgrading-to-vcf-5-2-1/ — checked the documented 4.5.2-to-5.2.1 planning milestone; the fixture has no Supervisor, so its Kubernetes-only detours do not apply.
+- VMware Cloud Foundation Blog, “How to Upgrade to VMware Cloud Foundation 9.1”: https://blogs.vmware.com/cloud-foundation/2026/06/18/how-to-upgrade-to-vmware-cloud-foundation-9-1/ — confirmed the 5.2.x-to-9.1 path, Aria Operations 8.18 prerequisite, SDDC Manager/NSX/vCenter/ESX/Edge finalization order, RDU for vCenter, image-managed ESX requirement, and management-services transition.
+- Broadcom Knowledge Base 312196, “VMware Cloud Foundation NSX-T Edge Node Virtual Machine Resizing Tool”: https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/312196/vmware-cloud-foundation-nsxt-edge-node-v.html — confirmed supported VCF Edge resize form factors, homogeneous sizing, one-at-a-time replacement behavior, and post-resize anti-affinity checks.
+
+Coverage: the interoperability matrix supplies compatibility and interoperability evidence; the knowledge-base articles and VCF upgrade guides supply upgrade guidance and product documentation for lifecycle sequencing, prerequisites, management services, and Edge resizing.
+
+The live material did not conflict with the frozen compatibility snapshot used to render the artifact.
